Subject: [PATCH] objtool: recognize Rust 1.92 panic_const symbols

Observed-Repository-Commit: 9438ad175b4c1ac7855f6afc119f154639fe18c2
Observed-Workflow: Native Rust host modules exact Rocky build
Observed-Run-ID: 31644047766
Observed-Job-ID: 94273299611
Observed-Artifact-ID: 9160078637
Observed-Artifact-Zip-Bytes: 62669
Observed-Artifact-Zip-SHA256: e4c3786f8fed3255fcd4f4c9e9baba340527050bf5be1b044b9c81cdd5a4cfbc
Observed-Rustc: 1.92.0
Rocky-Base: linux-6.12.0-211.44.1.el10_2
License: GPL-2.0-only

Rust 1.92 emits legacy-v0 `core::panicking::panic_const` symbols whose
function-name length component may be 23. The existing Objtool heuristic
recognizes only the length-24 form, so it treats calls to the new symbol as
returning and reports the caller as falling through into the next function.

Recognize the exact length-23 panic_const prefix observed while compiling the
native IHK module. Keep the existing length-24 match for other compiler output.
This is a project-observed compatibility patch; no upstream or stable commit is
claimed.

Signed-off-by: McKernel Rust Migration <mckernel@localhost>
---
 tools/objtool/check.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/tools/objtool/check.c b/tools/objtool/check.c
index dc24ceed3c7d..79ecc543a414 100644
--- a/tools/objtool/check.c
+++ b/tools/objtool/check.c
@@ -218,6 +218,7 @@ static bool is_rust_noreturn(const struct symbol *func)
 	       str_ends_with(func->name, "_4core9panicking36panic_misaligned_pointer_dereference")	||
 	       str_ends_with(func->name, "_7___rustc17rust_begin_unwind")				||
 	       strstr(func->name, "_4core9panicking13assert_failed")					||
+	       strstr(func->name, "_4core9panicking11panic_const23panic_const_")			||
 	       strstr(func->name, "_4core9panicking11panic_const24panic_const_")			||
 	       (strstr(func->name, "_4core5slice5index") &&
 		strstr(func->name, "slice_") &&
